# What must never be committed.
#
# The rule this file enforces: **nothing derived from your disk, and nothing
# Commodore's, goes into the repository.** The disassembly ships (a deliberate
# decision, see docs/DECISIONS.md); the game's data does not, because that is
# the part that would be redistributing somebody's copyright rather than
# describing it.
#
# There is exactly one exception and it is at the bottom.
#
# Kept as a tracked .gitignore rather than only in .git/info/exclude so the
# protection travels with the repository instead of living on one machine.

# --- your copy of the game, and everything decoded out of it ------------------
*.nib
*.g64
*.d64
*.t64
*.tap
*.crt
*.prg
*.seq
out/
*_files/

# --- the C64's own ROMs. Located at runtime, never vendored -------------------
# See assets.find_c64_rom: an installed VICE is searched automatically.
basic.bin
basic-*.bin
chargen.bin
chargen-*.bin
kernal.bin
kernal-*.bin

# --- audio, whether rendered from the SID or supplied by you ------------------
*.wav
*.sid
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.flac

# --- one player's own runs ----------------------------------------------------
settings.toml
settings.toml.bak
logs/

# --- working material that is not the project ---------------------------------
Archive/
archive/

# --- the usual Python and tooling debris --------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- editors and operating systems --------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- the AI assistant used to build this, and the working todo list -----------
# Nothing an end user needs to run the game or check the decompilation. The
# decompilation itself (docs/re/*, docs/DECISIONS.md, the disassembly listing)
# stays tracked on purpose - only the coding-assistant config and the running
# to-do list are excluded here.
.claude/
todo.md
docs/TODO_ARCHIVE.md

# --- THE ONE EXCEPTION --------------------------------------------------------
# The C64 character ROM's glyph bitmaps, generated by tools/embed_c64_font.py.
#
# Deliberately committed (owner's decision, 2026-08-30) so the loader screens
# are drawn in the real font on a machine with no emulator installed. It is the
# only place Commodore's data lives here, it is one file, and deleting it undoes
# the decision completely - `romfont` falls back to a system face and the tests
# cover both states.
#
# The negation has to come after `*.bin` and friends above, and the file is .py
# rather than .bin precisely so it is legible and diffable as source.
!src/alien_remake/render/c64font_data.py
